                                "sense_id": "db321687-87d2-36af-bef9-40785e4cce81",
                                "text": "Hildy S. Lipner, chief of pediatric speech pathology at Joseph M. Sanzari Children’s Hospital in Hackensack, N.J., said that by the time she sees children with picky eating problems, they are usually between 18 months and 3 years old and already have their patterns well established."
